meta {
  name: Import Radiology Master Data from Tenant
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/branch/import-radiology-from-tenant
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  The branch-admin "Import Master Data" action on the **Radiology** Master Data
  page: sync the tenant's **Tenant Master Data → the active branch's Branch Master
  Data**, radiology tests + panels (full overwrite). The radiology twin of
  `Import Master Data from Tenant`. Requires a branch-scoped token
  (`active_branch_id` from the JWT) — 400 otherwise.

  Update-or-create-or-delete keyed on provenance (`sourceMasterRadiologyTestId` /
  `sourceMasterRadiologyPanelId`, falling back to test/panel code): existing branch
  rows are fully overwritten from the tenant catalogue, missing ones are created,
  branch rows whose tenant source was removed are soft-deleted (unless hand-created
  / never synced). Panel membership is remapped to the branch radiology test copies.
  Runs as one transaction. Returns
  `{ tests: { created, updated, deleted }, panels: { created, updated, deleted } }`.

  The radiology model is FLAT (no samples/result-params), so — unlike the lab
  import — there are no child tables to rebuild. The branch radiology test/panel
  LISTS keep their own "Import / Sync Branch Radiology Tests" (`/branch-radiology-
  tests`), which is what Create Order reads; this endpoint only touches Branch
  Master Data.

  **Authorization:** reuses the lab Master-Data import permissions — requires ANY
  of `branch_admin:master_data__import_master_lab_tests` or
  `branch_admin:master_data__import_master_lab_panels` (no radiology-specific keys
  exist; business routes don't yet enforce route-level RBAC). `branch_admin` holds
  both by baseline; `business_admin`/`administrator` bypass.
}
